WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.948 --> 00:00:04.387
- I have to have a pretty girl.

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:08.998
If she's got no clothes
on, that's even better.

00:00:08.998 --> 00:00:13.165
I've worked for Playboy, I've
been doing that for 15 years.

00:00:14.027 --> 00:00:18.194
But I was the creator of the
Cheerios bee long, long ago.

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:25.176
I remember it as one of
the earliest things I did.

00:00:25.176 --> 00:00:29.146
The bee that I drew, I thought
it would be kind of fun

00:00:29.146 --> 00:00:31.552
to do one that looked more like a bee.

00:00:31.552 --> 00:00:35.525
So I gave him big
compound eyes and antennas

00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:38.005
and that wasn't at all what they wanted.

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:40.506
They thought he was a
little too insect-like,

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.816
and insects and cereal,

00:00:42.816 --> 00:00:46.496
it's probably not a good combination.

00:00:46.496 --> 00:00:50.663
But he eventually ended up
looking like he does now.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.056
We put shoes on him which I
didn't have in the beginning.

00:00:55.056 --> 00:00:57.896
Oh, and they gave him a sweater,

00:00:57.896 --> 00:01:00.026
so he was wearing something.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.859
- [Interviewer] So he really is more

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:03.386
like a Disney character than an insect?

00:01:03.386 --> 00:01:04.219
- Yes.

00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:08.386
I, I always say he looks like
Elmer Fudd in a bee suit.

00:01:09.546 --> 00:01:12.186
The face became more human.

00:01:12.186 --> 00:01:14.005
He got a little nose, of course.

00:01:14.005 --> 00:01:16.626
And eyes with pupils, no compound eyes.

00:01:16.626 --> 00:01:18.363
- [Interviewer] Why,
what is it with the eyes?

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:20.546
- [Dean] Well the eyes are the main thing.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:21.957
When you do a cartoon character,

00:01:21.957 --> 00:01:23.776
you want to focus on the eyes,

00:01:23.776 --> 00:01:26.837
after all and if you can have eye brows

00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:29.226
and eyes with pupils,

00:01:29.226 --> 00:01:32.726
you need something that can be expressive.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.413
- [Interviewer] Now you work for Playboy?

00:01:35.413 --> 00:01:37.275
- [Dean] Yes, yes.

00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:41.733
Hef said he liked my
Lady and the Tramp eyes.

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:44.983
I try to keep things a little innocent.

